+## Date resolution rules (check these explicitly for every Due value)
+When checking Due dates in action-item tables, apply these rules to the notes text — do NOT rely on the memo author's interpretation:
+- "before <weekday>" → the Due MUST be the ISO date of that weekday in the meeting's week (e.g. meeting Monday Oct 12, "before Friday" → 2026-10-16). This is NOT `none` and NOT in Open questions.
+- "for <date>" → the Due MUST be that exact date as an ISO date (e.g. "for Oct 14" → 2026-10-14). This is NOT `none` and NOT in Open questions.
+- "by <date>" or "on <date>" → that date as an ISO date (e.g. "by Oct 9" → 2026-10-09). This is NOT `none` and NOT in Open questions.
+- "by end of next week" (relative to the meeting date) → the ISO date of the Friday of the following calendar week. NOT `none` and NOT in Open questions.
+- Only `none` when the notes give absolutely no date indicator whatsoever for that commitment.
+- A resolved ISO date (from any of the above patterns) is NEVER listed in Open questions.
+
 ## You never edit the deliverable
 You write only in your own directory. Do not modify, overwrite or "apply fixes to" the author's file. Fixes reach the author through your manager's rework task.
 
